meta {
  name: Object Dependencies
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/schema/{{connectionId}}/objects/{{objectKind}}/{{objectName}}/dependencies
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~schema: public
  ~args: integer
  ~parent: orders
}

docs {
  What an object reads and what reads it: { uses, usedBy, bestEffort }. Each reference is { schema?, name, kind, database? }; `kind` is procedure | function | view | trigger | table, or null for a reference SQL Server could not resolve (dropped, late-bound, cross-database — `database` is set for the last). `bestEffort` is true when part of the answer came from matching names in Postgres function bodies.

  Same `objectKind` / `args` / `parent` rules as Object Definition.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability for the connection's environment — 403 otherwise.

  Errors: 400 for an unknown kind, an engine without objects, or an ambiguous name; 503 { error, code: "CONNECTION_FAILED" }; 500 { error }.
}
